    "id": 1550,
    "date": "2022-10-22T18:56:18+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "For bicycle people:\n\nCity cycling setup vs. long-distance cross country setup.  \n\nMy long-distance bicycle setup has been stripped down to the basics bags, fenders and racks.\n\nA secondary bicycle for local errands, picking up and delivering things.  \n\nOld-school, ten speed, lightweight cro-moly steel mixtee frame, also suitable rake for touring, but used with trailer in the city.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1551,
    "date": "2022-10-22T18:57:18+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Very beautiful autumn day in Upstate New York, the Mohawk Valley.",
    "media": null
  },
  {
    "id": 1552,
    "date": "2022-10-22T18:58:17+00:00",
    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "A short walk from my birth home, in Rome, New York.  Across the river is my old school, attended at the age of 14.\n\nIt is very beautiful in this part of the country, but most especially in the spring, summer, and fall.\n\nMany people are born here and live here all their lives.",
    "media": "1552.jpg"
